<div class="prose">
  <h3 class="t3">Still open</h3>
  <p>Loading the QML engine is 58 ms and I have taken it apart: 4 ms to warm the engine, 6 for the Controls import, 14 for the toolbar, 9 for the file view container, 7 for the sidebar, and so on down to nothing. There is no hotspot. It is a user interface with a lot of buttons in it, and the only way to make it cheaper is to build less of it before the first frame.</p>
  <p>Which leads to the number I find funniest in the whole log. At the first frame the window contains 662 items, and 257 of them are invisible. Thirty-nine percent of the interface is built to not be seen: a hidden text item per file used only to measure whether a filename fits on two lines, whichever of the icon or the thumbnail is not currently showing, two inactive badge loaders per row. That is worth about 2 ms and a lighter row while scrolling. It is recorded as a finding, not shipped as a change, because I ran out of week.</p>
  <p>Also open: the settings window's first open at 85 ms, about 60 of which is creating a swapchain for a second top level window, the AppImage's FUSE tax, and one clipboard call that is still synchronous on an explicit paste.</p>
  <p>The long version of this log, with commit hashes and the measurements in the order they happened, lives in the HyprFM repository as <code>docs/performance-history.md</code>. It is less polite than this sheet.</p>
</div>
